From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FE Fates port <port@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 03:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 0022] core: Fire Emblem Fates: a mod's chapter person file numbers its people in file order

A battle save writes each unit's person as its number (Person+0x24,
Person::SerializePointer 0x0044A54C) and Person::DeserializePointer
(0x0044A62C) takes the record at (number - the first record's number)
back: by position. Every person file of the game numbers its records in
file order; Seal of Flames v6's R021, R023 and Y004 carry the same
numbers in another order, so after a battle-save reload those units
became the person at their number's position (same class, level and
place; another person and HP), with the randomizer off too. The mod
layer's person fix (0018) now also serves such a file numbered in file
order from its first record's number, only when the numbers are exactly
that range in another order. fates_person_name becomes fates_person_fix
(name and numbers). Round 60, track sealfix: docs/tests/SEAL_SAVE.md 8.
